## 4. User Roles & Journeys

### 4.1 Super Admin
**Journey:** Full system access — configure costs, manage all users, view all tickets, manage elections, view reports.  
**Key Actions:** Create users, configure pricing, manage representatives, view financial analytics.

### 4.2 Admin (Manager/Staff/Lead)
**Journey:** Day-to-day operations — review pending tickets, assign clerks, update statuses, process wallet top-ups.  
**Key Actions:** Assign pending tickets → track progress → mark completed → manage finance.

### 4.3 Consumer
**Journey:** Request legal document services, pay via wallet, track ticket status.  
**Key Actions:** Select service → fill form → pay → track ticket → receive documents.

### 4.4 Lawyer
**Journey:** Similar to consumer but may have specialized professional services or rates.

### 4.5 Representative (Clerk)
**Journey:** Receive assigned tickets → physically obtain documents from courts → mark complete.  
**Key Actions:** View assigned tickets → update in-progress status → upload delivery proof → mark completed.

### 4.6 Investor / Company
**Journey:** Monitoring/investment roles (exact features TBD — may have custom dashboards).

---

## 5. Key Workflows

### 5.1 Ticket Creation Workflow
```
Consumer/Admin → Paralegal Services → Select Category (Judicial/Non-Judicial)
→ Select Service Type → Multi-step form (4–5 steps) → Submit
→ Ticket created (Pending status) → Admin assigns clerk
→ Clerk marks "In Progress" → Clerk delivers → Marks "Completed"
```

### 5.2 Payment Workflow
```
Consumer needs to pay → Admin processes wallet top-up
→ Consumer sends money (JazzCash/EasyPaisa/Bank)
→ Admin uploads receipt and verifies → Wallet credited
→ Wallet balance deducted when ticket completed
```

### 5.3 Representative Assignment Workflow
```
Admin views Pending Tickets → Opens Ticket Panel
→ Selects "Assign Representative" → Filters by service/city → Assigns clerk
→ Ticket moves to "Assigned" → Clerk sees ticket in their queue
→ Clerk starts work → Updates to "In Progress"
→ Clerk completes → Admin verifies → "Completed"
```

